    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Google Lyria is an API only line for turning image and text input into audio and text output, with no open weights anywhere in the family. Both listed versions, Lyria 3 Pro Preview and Lyria 3 Clip Preview, share a context window of 1048576 tokens and a maximum output of 65536 tokens, and both are priced at $0 per million input and output tokens. Neither version supports reasoning. The facts suggest the family suits audio generation tasks that need long inputs and generous outputs, such as producing clips from large image and text prompts, and the zero listed price makes cost a non issue for these two versions. The limits are the lack of reasoning, the absence of open weights, and the fact that only two preview versions are listed, so the family is narrow and API bound.",
